{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-refueling-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.58: `project-refueling`, a PROJECT-domain run of the REFUELING losses, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its PROJECT input database (`inputs/washtenaw-project-crankcase.esm`, shared with `project-crankcase`). It selects source types 21 (gasoline) and 62 (diesel), road types 4 and 5, and THC and TOG for refueling displacement vapor loss (18) and spillage (19); MOVES adds their Total Energy parents (running 9101, start 9102, extended idle 9190) as prerequisites and strips them from the output, and writes no TOG row, as in `process-refueling`. Its 418 MOVESOutput rows are THC displacement (gasoline and E85 passenger cars) and spillage (those and diesel cars and trucks) on link 1 (road type 4) and link 2 (road type 5).\n\nWHAT IT EXERCISES: RefuelingLossCalculator copies each Total Energy row of running, start, extended idle or APU at its own link and road type times a rate over the fuel's energy content and density, and tests no domain (`rspp_copiesParentRows`). The run selects no off-network road type, so start and extended idle have no row anywhere and every refueling row is running energy's on its link. The pre-port model refused the run (`run_domainUnported` = 2) and was wrong on the long-haul trucks' spillage by 25-63%: it carried ProjectTAG's hotelling hours into an extended-idle energy block on road types 4 and 5, where extended idle does not occur, and the chain added that block to the trucks' refueling. A hotelling block's weight is now zero where its process does not occur on the road (`ppr_occursOnRoad`), as a start block's already was; no earlier run reads such a block.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 418. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
